{"name":"Moray Eel","hex":"#00a78b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moray eel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various brightly colored marine eels of the family Muraenidae, of warm coastal waters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moray_eel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moray eel","blocks":[{"text":"Moray eels, or Muraenidae, are a family of eels whose members are found worldwide. There are approximately 200 species in 16 genera which are almost exclusively marine, but several species are regularly seen in brackish water, and a few are found in fresh water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Moray_eel.jpg/330px-Moray_eel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moray_eel","wikidata":"Q35076"},{"title":"Moray","blocks":[{"text":"Moray is one of the 32 council areas of Scotland. It lies in the north-east of the country, with a coastline on the Moray Firth, and borders the council areas of Aberdeenshire and Highland. Its council is based in Elgin, the area's largest town. The main towns are generally in the north of the area on the coastal plain. The south of the area is more sparsely populated and mountainous, including part of the Cairngorms National Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Moray_UK_location_map.svg/330px-Moray_UK_location_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moray","wikidata":"Q211106"},{"title":"Eel","blocks":[{"text":"Eels are ray-finned fish belonging to the order Anguilliformes, which consists of eight suborders, 20 families, 164 genera, and about 1000 species. Eels undergo considerable development from the early larval stage to the eventual adult stage and are usually predators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/New_Zealand_longfin_eel_%28A